trong Republican turnout operation could compress the four-point polling gap in this competitive district.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Chris Pappas (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Hampshire's 1st District is an open seat this cycle, with Democrat Stefany Shaheen facing Republican Anthony DiLorenzo after Chris Pappas left the seat to run for Senate. The district leans Democratic by about two points, and the broader 2026 environment favors Democrats. Two recent polls of likely voters, from Saint Anselm College and the University of New Hampshire, both show Shaheen ahead by four points.\n\nExpert raters overwhelmingly call the race Likely Democratic, with one rating it Safe D and one Lean D. Prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket both price Shaheen's chances at about 93 percent. DiLorenzo has raised more money directly, but outside spending has flowed heavily in Shaheen's favor. The race remains competitive on paper, but the weight of the evidence points to a Democratic hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.937, "margin": 10.01}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9238, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9245, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8928, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8695, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.844, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.871, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8487, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8802, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8452, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8807, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8831, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8873, "margin": 7.2}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8466, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8765, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8928, "margin": 8.0}, {"date"